<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/admin-console.css" />
</head>

<body>
  <%- include('_menu', { page: 'users', user: user }) %>

  <main class="admin-shell">
    <div class="admin-head">
      <h2>People</h2>
      <p class="admin-lede">
        Everybody With an Account. Nearly All of Them Are Ordinary Users, Who
        Search for Rooms and Save Favourites; a Few Maintain the Map Itself.
        Only an Administrator Can Appoint Another One, and Nobody Can Stand
        Themselves Down — so the Campus Is Never Left Without One.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="admin-block">
      <div class="admin-head-row">
        <h3>Accounts <span class="admin-count" id="userCount">0</span></h3>
        <input type="search" id="userFilter" class="admin-filter"
               placeholder="Filter by name or address…" autocomplete="off"
               aria-label="Filter accounts">
      </div>
      <p class="admin-note" id="userState">Loading…</p>

      <table class="admin-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Account</th>
            <th scope="col">Role</th>
            <th scope="col">Last Signed In</th>
            <th scope="col"></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="userRows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="admin-block">
      <h3>How Somebody Becomes an Administrator</h3>
      <ul class="admin-points">
        <li>
          <strong>Appointed Here.</strong> Any Administrator Can Make Another
          One, and Stand Any of the Others Down. The Change Is Written to the
          Firebase Account Itself — There Is No Second List Anywhere — and the
          Person Is Signed Out, So Their Next Sign-In Starts With It.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Never by Themselves.</strong> What Marks an Administrator Can
          Only Be Written by This Server, So Being Appointed Is Always
          Something Done to an Account Rather Than by It. Nobody Can Stand
          Themselves Down Either, So the Campus Is Never Left Without One.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The First One.</strong> On a New Deployment Nobody Is an
          Administrator Yet and This Page Cannot Be Reached, so the First Is
          Appointed on the Server:
          <code>node scripts/make-admin.js someone@bcit.ca</code>. That Is Also
          the Way Back if Every Administrator Is Removed.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script defer type="module" src="/js/admin-users.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
